course: dictionary
lesson: 7494
title: Words that change with place
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A postbox is a box where you post letters so they can be collected and sent. Once you know that, a sentence about a postbox is easy to follow.
explain: In the sentence «Kieran from her own street stared at her in class and went red as a postbox whenever she looked back», the words «red as a postbox» are a comparison. They tell you that Kieran's face went very red, probably from embarrassment, because he was staring. Always ask: what is being compared, and why?
explain: Some words change with the place you live. In Britain and Ireland, postbox is the usual word for the box on the street. In the USA and Canada, people say «mailbox». Postboxes are red in the UK, Australia and New Zealand, but green in Ireland, so check where the story is set.
fact: A postbox is a public box where you put letters to be collected and sent.
fact: In the UK, Australia and New Zealand, postboxes are usually red. In Ireland they are green.
fact: Postbox can also mean a private box at your house or at a post office where your own post is delivered.
fact: In the USA and Canada, people usually say «mailbox» instead of postbox.
fact: «Red as a postbox» is a simile, which compares two things using as. It means very red.
exercise: In «went red as a postbox», what is being compared to a postbox? | The bus stop | The school door | Her letter | *Kieran's face
exercise: Which country usually paints its postboxes green? | New Zealand | *Ireland | UK | Australia
exercise: In the USA, what do people more often say instead of postbox? | Postcard | Letterbox | Pillar | *Mailbox
test: Mum says, «Take this letter to the nearest postbox.» What should Sam do? | Keep it in a drawer until Friday | Hide it under his bed | *Put the letter in the public box on the street | Read it aloud to the bus driver
test: Which box is used in the street to collect letters for posting? | Staircase | Wardrobe | *Postbox | Playground
exam: Which meaning fits «postbox» in a story about sending a letter to Father Christmas? | A box for toys | A football net | A wooden chest | *A box where you put letters to be collected
